// Subtitle translations for the tutorial narration.
//
// These are narration, not interface copy, so they live here instead of the app's
// i18n tables — adding them there would drag them into the i18n coverage contract
// and make every future voice-over tweak a translation emergency across the UI.
//
// English is not listed: it is the spoken language and is read straight from
// shots.mjs, so the script and its subtitles can never disagree.
//
// The language list is the twelve the cinematic tutorial offered, since this video
// replaces it. `youtube` is the BCP-47 tag YouTube expects when the caption file is
// uploaded — notably `zh-Hans` rather than a bare `zh`.
//
// A language with no entry falls back to English *and is reported* by
// subtitles.mjs; a half-translated file must never look finished.

